An Excel pivot with columns but no values ends at the column items

Excel lays out a pivot table with only column fields and no value
field as two rows: the column header and the column items. Calc keeps
a third, empty data row below them ("single row will remain empty").
The output clears its whole area before writing, so every refresh and
every save erased the user's cells in that row, and the export wrote
the table one row taller than Excel's (Ely R15.11l). For a pivot from
an Excel file (it has a column caption, patch 0071) with column fields
and no row or value field, the table now ends at the column items row;
the data area gets no style and no frame. Calc's own pivots keep their
layout.

